  "holistic_F_N": 3,
  "holistic_F_H": -3,
  "section_notes": "The final rules adopt a 55 °C test with a 5% corrective-action trigger and a 7% sales bar, so Northwind's Hearth 10 (6.2%) remains sellable; per-model results go to customers but are not public. S5 mandates recall above 8/100k with no phase-in, which would ban Halcyon's Ember 8 (9.9/100k). S3 retrofit is six years and S4 suppression is 36 months, satisfying the remaining red lines."
